  "briefing": [
    "International Night Train 417 is running north through the dark toward Belgrade. Its sleeping car left Veles almost full, stopped at Skopje across midnight, called at Kumanovo and Tabanovce, and is now standing under the white border lamps at Preševo. Some passengers are asleep. Others have already stepped off into the night.",
    "At 01:52, sleeper attendant Emil Stojanov opened Compartment 6 to return a passport and found Damjan Ristev, fifty-two, dead beside the lower berth. Damjan had a single narrow puncture wound beneath his left shoulder. There was no weapon in the room.",
    "The compartment appeared impossible. Its sliding door was locked, the brass privacy bolt was thrown from inside and the window was latched. Border officers forced the emergency release only after Damjan failed to answer. Nothing large enough for a person connects the compartment to the corridor or the track.",
    "Damjan was a claims investigator travelling to a civil inquiry in Belgrade. He had spent months reopening the 2011 Demir Kapija sleeper fire, in which one of two sisters died. Witnesses saw him carrying a red document folio before Skopje. The folio is missing, and the passengers disagree about whom he intended to name in his report.",
    "Train 417 cannot remain at the border until daylight. Reconstruct the stops, decide whether the locked compartment was truly the scene of the attack, and identify which passenger left the train with a reason to silence Damjan Ristev."
  ],
